sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Op as Operator screen
  participant S as Supervisor
  participant L as Locomotion
  Note over S,L: Robot is driving along a row,<br/>or turning to the next row.<br/>It must stay on the beam and reach the right spot.
  S->>L: CMD_START (drive to spot 14 of the row)
  L-->>S: FAULT (OFF_BEAM, CANNOT_REACH_SPOT or TURN_FAILED), wheels stopped
  S->>L: CMD_START (retry 1 of 2, relocate to beam)
  L-->>S: FAULT
  S->>L: CMD_START (retry 2 of 2, relocate to beam)
  L-->>S: FAULT
  S->>Op: ALERT: robot stopped. Spot 14, Locomotion, fault code
  Note over S: Stack light turns flashing amber, so the operator sees it from across the roof
  Note over S: Robot waits where it is.<br/>There is no skip, because later spots depend on being on the beam.
  Op->>S: RESOLVED (robot placed back on beam)
  S->>L: CMD_START (resume driving)
  L-->>S: DONE
